      "id": 8,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "About this dashboard",
      "gridPos": {"h": 7, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 14},
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "# Polaris POC — Grafana view\n\nThis dashboard pulls from the `polaris-postgres` datasource, which points\nat the `pol_customer` database on the host Postgres. It is intentionally\nread-only; the customer portal is what enforces tenant isolation at\nthe application layer, and Grafana is a second vantage point that\nproves the data is accessible to an authenticated Admin (like `carol`)\nbut cannot be manipulated.\n\n## What each panel shows\n\n- **Total tenants** — rows in the `tenants` table (acme, brightside,\n  partners in the seed).\n- **Total customer rows** — rows in `customer_data` across all tenants.\n- **Active tenant groups** — distinct tenant_ids that have at least one\n  row (matches the number of customer tenants).\n- **Seed users** — the count of OIDC users in the Keycloak realm\n  (hard-coded to 6 for this POC).\n- **Rows per tenant** — barchart showing how the rows distribute.\n- **All customer_data rows** — table view of every row, with tenant\n  name resolved. The customer portal would only show rows for the\n  user's own tenant; Grafana (as Admin) sees all of them.\n\n## Access control\n\nThe Admin role is required to view this dashboard because the panels\nread directly from the database without the RLS context. The Admin\ngroup is `pol-admin`, which the JMESPath in\n`GF_AUTH_GENERIC_OAUTH_ROLE_ATTRIBUTE_PATH` maps to Grafana Admin.\n"
      }
    }
